Consume successive /?
/ delimiters in order. Preserve the incomplete suffix until flush; on final flush process a nonempty suffix exactly once. A bare CR is not a delimiter. A line beginning with space or tab is a continuation. Otherwise a header matches exactly /^([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*(?:\[[^\]
]*\])?(?:\{[^
]*\})?):(?:\s?(.*))?$/ with source JavaScript regex semantics. Name is capture 1 before its first '[' or '{'. inline is capture 2 trimmed nonempty. Every other line is a continuation: remove exactly two initial spaces, otherwise one initial tab, otherwise none. Header inline values are decoded by structured-inline-value; subsequent field ownership is exclusively structuredStreamState.md.
